[5] Proof readout
  1. The 15 residual coarse ET+unit route-mixed fibers are finite
     and all 38 packets in them are strict-open.
  2. Arc topology alone separates most residual route collisions,
     but some same-topology Q/covering pairs need a stalk or
     magnitude/nested-refinement tooth.
  3. The exact safe-component stalk and magnitude cocycle separate
     every residual fiber without invoking boundary/open status.
  4. Therefore the next proof object can be a residual tooth manifest:
     for each coarse gate fiber, record the first legal non-route
     tooth before falling back to explicit q/covering certificate labels.
